This image implements the TC2 dispatcher for the Track D layout using the
Track B graph.  The safety policy is fail-closed: a train is not launched
unless its route, braking/reversal guards, sensor service, reservation
generation, and CAN transport are all healthy.

## Build and test

On `linux.student.cs`:

```text
make clean
make
```

`MODE=TC2` is the default and produces `iotest.img`.  An explicit build is:

```text
make clean
make MODE=TC2
```

Target warnings are build failures; a demo image is not produced from a
warning-bearing AArch64 compile.

The final line must be:

```text
Built and verified MODE=TC2 image: iotest.img
```

The linked-image gate also requires this runtime build marker:

```text
TC2 build marker: stage60-paired-stop-reroute
```

TC1, TC2, and PERF use separate `build/<MODE>/<config-id>/` object trees.  The
configuration id includes the source set and tool/compile/link
flags, the normal default ignores an ambient shell `MODE`, and the final link
is rejected unless the requested mode's symbols and banner are present.  The
root `iotest.elf` and `iotest.img` are copies of the verified selected-mode
artifacts.

Host regression tests use Clang with AddressSanitizer and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer:

```text
make test
```

The tests cover route candidates and unavailable segments, a complete
stop/reverse/turnout/resume/outbound-sensor path,
asynchronous turnout preparation and repeated queue backpressure,
2/3/4/6-command launch waves, ordered sensor monitoring, sliding reservations,
all 128 exact directed-side-to-D and all 64 estimated D-to-D `CURRENT`
planning/convergence cases, two-evidence relocalization,
destination-and-generation compare-and-swap plan replacement,
retained CAN batch status, emergency-stop ordering and retry,
CAN/MCP2515 transport, terminal blocking behavior, and the fallback motion
model, plus exhaustive speed-1..120 provisional prediction monotonicity and
T14/A/d7 isolation.  The course
AArch64 toolchain is still required for the linked image; host Clang tests are
